From: SenkOS
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: H616: pick LPDDR3 or LPDDR4 by the boot0 DRAM straps

Anbernic H700 boards carry LPDDR4 or LPDDR3. Allwinner's boot0 reads PH6,
PH7, PH8 and PH10 with pull-ups and uses the result as an index into its
DRAM parameter sets: 0 and 15 LPDDR4, 14 LPDDR3 (1-13 DDR3).

SUNXI_DRAM_H616_LPDDR3_STRAPS builds the LPDDR3 timings next to the
LPDDR4 ones, reads the straps before DRAM init and, for LPDDR3, raises
DCDC3 to 1.2 V and uses boot0's LPDDR3 parameters with the DX delays
ROCKNIX's LPDDR3 builds use.

To make that possible, the PHY init tables are picked by the DRAM type at
runtime, and ns_to_t() takes the clock from the parameters (as boot0
does) instead of CONFIG_DRAM_CLK.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.h b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.h
index a8fdda12..315533f8 100644
--- a/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/asm/arch-sunxi/dram_sun50i_h616.h
@@ -168,13 +168,14 @@ struct dram_config {
 	u8 bus_full_width;
 };
 
-static inline int ns_to_t(int nanoseconds)
+static inline int ns_to_t(const struct dram_para *para, int nanoseconds)
 {
-	const unsigned int ctrl_freq = CONFIG_DRAM_CLK / 2;
+	const unsigned int ctrl_freq = para->clk / 2;
 
 	return DIV_ROUND_UP(ctrl_freq * nanoseconds, 1000);
 }
 
 void mctl_set_timing_params(const struct dram_para *para);
+void mctl_set_timing_params_lpddr3(const struct dram_para *para);
 
 #endif /* _SUNXI_DRAM_SUN50I_H616_H */
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
index f984ea29..470aa043 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -714,6 +714,15 @@ config SUNXI_DRAM_A523_LPDDR4
 	  This option is the LPDDR4 timing used by the stock boot0 by
 	  Allwinner.
 endchoice
+
+config SUNXI_DRAM_H616_LPDDR3_STRAPS
+	bool "Also support LPDDR3 boards, told apart by the boot0 DRAM straps"
+	depends on DRAM_SUN50I_H616 && SUNXI_DRAM_H616_LPDDR4 && AXP717_POWER
+	help
+	  Anbernic H700 boards carry LPDDR4 or LPDDR3. Allwinner's boot0 picks
+	  its DRAM parameters by straps on PH6, PH7, PH8 and PH10. With this,
+	  SPL reads them and initializes LPDDR3 at 1.2 V (DCDC3) when they say
+	  so, LPDDR4 otherwise.
 endif
 
 config DRAM_TYPE
